    "summary": "Electric deep blues & fierce The Other One jam dominate",
    "blurb": "The all‑electric set is anchored by a scorching The Other One > Not Fade Away sequence and an extended Hard To Handle jam. Deep Elem Blues gets a rare electric treatment, while Sugar Magnolia and Candyman shine. The second audience tape offers the clearest listening experience.",
    "review": "On October 10, 1970 at Queens’ Colden Auditorium the Dead delivered a pure‑electric marathon that still feels vivid despite the limitations of audience‑sourced tapes. Highlights include an intense The Other One > Not Fade Away segue that rolls into a muscular jam, a hard‑driving Hard To Handle stretch, and a seldom‑heard electric rendition of Deep Elem Blues where Jerry’s tentative vocal adds a quirky charm while his guitar soars through the improvisations. The first set closes with a tight Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One transition that keeps the momentum high before winding down into a relaxed second set featuring classics like Casey Jones and Uncle John’s Band. While both tapes suffer from typical 1970 audience hiss and occasional drop‑outs, the Sony F‑95 cassette capture (gd1970-10-10.144636.sony-f95.lee.hance.sirmick.flac1648) presents a noticeably clearer picture of the band’s interplay, making it the preferred version for most listeners.",
